<header>
<h1>MSYS2</h1>
<h2>Software Distribution and Building Platform for Windows</h2>
</header>

<h1 id=3D"_1"></h1>
<p><strong>MSYS2</strong> is a collection of tools and libraries providing =
you with an
easy-to-use environment for building, installing and running native Windows
software.</p>
<p>It consists of a command line terminal called
<a href=3D"https://mintty.github.io/">mintty</a>, bash, version control sys=
tems like git and
subversion, tools like tar and awk and even build systems like autotools, a=
ll
based on a modified version of <a href=3D"https://cygwin.com/">Cygwin</a>. =
Despite some of
these central parts being based on Cygwin, the main focus of MSYS2 is to pr=
ovide
a build environment for native Windows software and the Cygwin-using parts =
are
kept at a minimum. MSYS2 provides up-to-date native builds for GCC, mingw-w=
64,
CPython, CMake, Meson, OpenSSL, FFmpeg, Rust, Ruby, just to name a few.</p>
<p>To provide easy installation of packages and a way to keep them updated =
it
features a package management system called
<a href=3D"https://wiki.archlinux.org/index.php/pacman">Pacman</a>, which s=
hould be familiar
to Arch Linux users. It brings many powerful features such as dependency
resolution and simple complete system upgrades, as well as straight-forward=
 and
reproducible package building. Our package repository contains <a href=3D"h=
ttps://packages.msys2.org/base">more than 3700
pre-built packages</a> ready to install.</p>
<p>For more details see <a href=3D"https://www.msys2.org/docs/what-is-msys2=
/">'What is MSYS2?'</a> which also
compares MSYS2 to other software distributions and development environments=
 like
<a href=3D"https://cygwin.com/">Cygwin</a>,
<a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Windows_Subsystem_for_Linux">WSL</=
a>,
<a href=3D"https://chocolatey.org/">Chocolatey</a>, <a href=3D"https://scoo=
p.sh/">Scoop</a>, ... and <a href=3D"https://www.msys2.org/docs/who-is-usin=
g-msys2/">'Who
Is Using MSYS2?'</a> to see which projects are using
MSYS2 and what for.</p>
<h2 id=3D"installation">Installation</h2>
<ol>
<li>
<p>Download the installer:
    </p><div class=3D"download-section"><a href=3D"https://github.com/msys2=
/msys2-installer/releases/download/2026-06-11/msys2-x86_64-20260611.exe" cl=
ass=3D"button"><span class=3D"twemoji"><svg xmlns=3D"http://www.w3.org/2000=
/svg" viewBox=3D"0 0 16 16"><path d=3D"M2.75 14A1.75 1.75 0 0 1 1 12.25v-2.=
5a.75.75 0 0 1 1.5 0v2.5c0 .138.112.25.25.25h10.5a.25.25 0 0 0 .25-.25v-2.5=
a.75.75 0 0 1 1.5 0v2.5A1.75 1.75 0 0 1 13.25 14Z"></path><path d=3D"M7.25 =
7.689V2a.75.75 0 0 1 1.5 0v5.689l1.97-1.969a.749.749 0 1 1 1.06 1.06l-3.25 =
3.25a.75.75 0 0 1-1.06 0L4.22 6.78a.749.749 0 1 1 1.06-1.06z"></path></svg>=
</span> msys2-x86_64-20260611.exe</a> or <a href=3D"https://github.com/msys=
2/msys2-installer/releases/download/2026-06-11/msys2-arm64-20260611.exe" cl=
ass=3D"button"><span class=3D"twemoji"><svg xmlns=3D"http://www.w3.org/2000=
/svg" viewBox=3D"0 0 16 16"><path d=3D"M2.75 14A1.75 1.75 0 0 1 1 12.25v-2.=
5a.75.75 0 0 1 1.5 0v2.5c0 .138.112.25.25.25h10.5a.25.25 0 0 0 .25-.25v-2.5=
a.75.75 0 0 1 1.5 0v2.5A1.75 1.75 0 0 1 13.25 14Z"></path><path d=3D"M7.25 =
7.689V2a.75.75 0 0 1 1.5 0v5.689l1.97-1.969a.749.749 0 1 1 1.06 1.06l-3.25 =
3.25a.75.75 0 0 1-1.06 0L4.22 6.78a.749.749 0 1 1 1.06-1.06z"></path></svg>=
</span> msys2-arm64-20260611.exe</a> (ARM64)</div><p></p>
<p><span style=3D"opacity: 0.6; word-wrap: break-word;">(Optional) For more=
 information on the installer, like command line options, or how to verify =
the checksum and signature of the installer, see the <a href=3D"https://www=
.msys2.org/docs/installer/">installer guide</a>.</span></p>
</li>
<li>
<p>Run the installer. Installing MSYS2 requires 64 bit Windows 10 (1809+) o=
r newer.</p>
</li>
<li>
<p>Enter your desired <strong>Installation Folder</strong>. We recommend us=
ing the default,
   see <a href=3D"https://www.msys2.org/docs/installer/#what-are-the-instal=
lation-folder-recommendations">installation folder
   recommendations</a>
   for more information.</p>
<p><img alt=3D"Second screen of MSYS2 installation" src=3D"https://www.msys=
2.org/images/install-2-path.png#gh-light-mode-only">
<img alt=3D"Second screen of MSYS2 installation" src=3D"https://www.msys2.o=
rg/images/install-2-path-dark.png#gh-dark-mode-only"></p>
</li>
<li>
<p>When done, click <strong>Finish</strong>.</p>
<p><img alt=3D"Third screen of MSYS2 installation" src=3D"https://www.msys2=
.org/images/install-3-finish.png#gh-light-mode-only">
<img alt=3D"Third screen of MSYS2 installation" src=3D"https://www.msys2.or=
g/images/install-3-finish-dark.png#gh-dark-mode-only"></p>
</li>
<li>
<p>Now MSYS2 is ready for you and a terminal for the <a href=3D"https://www=
.msys2.org/docs/environments/">UCRT64 environment</a> will launch.</p>
<p><img alt=3D"Empty MSYS2 terminal window" src=3D"https://www.msys2.org/im=
ages/install-4-terminal.png#gh-light-mode-only">
<img alt=3D"Empty MSYS2 terminal window" src=3D"https://www.msys2.org/image=
s/install-4-terminal-dark.png#gh-dark-mode-only"></p>
</li>
<li>
<p>You will probably want to install some tools like the mingw-w64 GCC to s=
tart compiling projects. Run the following command:</p>
<div class=3D"highlight"><pre id=3D"__code_0"><span></span><nav class=3D"md=
-code__nav"><button class=3D"md-code__button" title=3D"Copy to clipboard" d=
ata-clipboard-target=3D"#__code_0 &gt; code" data-md-type=3D"copy"></button=
></nav><code><span class=3D"gp">$ </span>pacman<span class=3D"w"> </span>-S=
<span class=3D"w"> </span>mingw-w64-ucrt-x86_64-gcc
</code></pre></div>
</li>
<li>
<p>The terminal window will show the output as below. Press 'Enter' to cont=
inue:</p>
<div class=3D"highlight"><pre id=3D"__code_1"><span></span><nav class=3D"md=
-code__nav"><button class=3D"md-code__button" title=3D"Copy to clipboard" d=
ata-clipboard-target=3D"#__code_1 &gt; code" data-md-type=3D"copy"></button=
></nav><code><span class=3D"go">resolving dependencies...</span>
<span class=3D"go">looking for conflicting packages...</span>

